WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:01.258 --> 00:00:03.677
["The Windmills Of Your Mind" playing]

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:00:12.686 --> 00:00:14.146
[patrons chattering]

4
00:00:22.112 --> 00:00:23.822
[Peg] Ay!

5
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.162
[financier] …chat to all of our clients.
and then we'll. uh. fix everything.

6
00:00:32.873 --> 00:00:34.082
See ya.

7
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.126
Where ya going?

8
00:00:39.087 --> 00:00:40.255
I'm going home?

9
00:00:40.839 --> 00:00:41.840
Yes.

10
00:00:42.382 --> 00:00:46.386
Um… As described
in the Sixth Provided Rules of Behavior.

11
00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.347
"To lie. defraud. or in any other way
manipulate human beings

12
00:00:49.431 --> 00:00:52.058
or human institutions for the sole purpose
of self-enrichment."

13
00:00:52.142 --> 00:00:53.435
What do you call yourself?

14
00:00:53.518 --> 00:00:54.644
I'm Sugar.

15
00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:58.356
Then give me a break with that shit.
Sugar. I know what I've done.

16
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.150
["Coming Home" playing]

17
00:01:08.658 --> 00:01:09.910
Hmm.

18
00:01:12.287 --> 00:01:13.497
You just get here?

19
00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:16.291
- Uh. few weeks.
- And?

20
00:01:16.374 --> 00:01:17.876
How does this compare?

21
00:01:17.959 --> 00:01:19.044
[breathes deeply]

22
00:01:19.753 --> 00:01:21.213
Ah. it's interesting.

23
00:01:22.339 --> 00:01:24.591
- Yeah?
- Yeah. I mean. I haven't seen a lot

24
00:01:24.674 --> 00:01:26.760
and. you know. I haven't traveled much.

25
00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.262
I haven't chosen an employment. But it's…

26
00:01:30.430 --> 00:01:31.473
it's interesting.

27
00:01:31.556 --> 00:01:34.684
I chose kindergarten teacher.
and I loved it.

28
00:01:34.768 --> 00:01:38.355
"Mrs. Rosenthal.
Good morning. Mrs. Rosenthal."

29
00:01:38.438 --> 00:01:41.274
I mean. they taught me more than anything.

30
00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.697
And one day during nap time.

31
00:01:47.781 --> 00:01:49.741
I was poking around
on the school computer.

32
00:01:49.825 --> 00:01:55.455
and I was exposed to what they call
the financial markets. and I was hooked.

33
00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:56.540
That was that.

34
00:01:57.791 --> 00:01:59.000
All of a sudden.

35
00:01:59.084 --> 00:02:03.797
finger painting with six-year-olds
was not that interesting anymore.

36
00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:06.466
What's finger painting?

37
00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:08.801
Oh. where… where they dip
their hands in color.

38
00:02:08.884 --> 00:02:11.012
- and then they draw with their fingers.
- [chuckles]

39
00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.431
So. I stopped teaching.

40
00:02:12.514 --> 00:02:14.599
I started a hedge fund and then…

41
00:02:14.683 --> 00:02:16.351
- [server] You know what you'd like?
- Papaya?

42
00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:19.688
- No papaya.
- Toast. dry. no butter. no jellies.

43
00:02:19.771 --> 00:02:22.649
- And no cinnamon. I'm allergic.
- I'll have a Caesar salad.

44
00:02:22.732 --> 00:02:26.695
a hanger steak with crinkle fries
and green beans.

45
00:02:26.778 --> 00:02:30.574
And yes. I am ignoring the rule
against consumption of animal meat.

46
00:02:30.657 --> 00:02:32.117
I'm sorry?

47
00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.368
Talking to him.

48
00:02:33.452 --> 00:02:36.621
For dessert. do you like
the ladyfingers or the chocolate torta?

49
00:02:36.705 --> 00:02:39.624
- Uh…
- One of each. but no cinnamon.

50
00:02:39.708 --> 00:02:41.042
I have the same allergy.

51
00:02:48.842 --> 00:02:50.343
We should be honoring these bodies.

52
00:02:50.427 --> 00:02:51.762
I have been…

53
00:02:52.596 --> 00:02:54.055
by giving it what it wants.

54
00:02:55.348 --> 00:02:56.892
It all works. you know.

55
00:02:57.476 --> 00:02:59.227
In case you ever get curious.

56
00:03:05.692 --> 00:03:06.860
It's good you're going home.

57
00:03:08.612 --> 00:03:10.071
[phone rings]

58
00:03:11.364 --> 00:03:12.449
Oh. excuse me.

59
00:03:13.784 --> 00:03:14.785
There you go.

60
00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:16.536
- If you need anything else. let me know.
- Mmm.

61
00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.621
Hi.

62
00:03:19.164 --> 00:03:20.415
Yeah. I love you.

63
00:03:27.839 --> 00:03:29.633
[grunts] My sister.

64
00:03:31.885 --> 00:03:33.386
So what are you thinking job-wise?

65
00:03:35.222 --> 00:03:38.475
Maybe a psychologist.
something with animals.

66
00:03:38.558 --> 00:03:39.768
Okay. what else?

67
00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:41.895
Hmm… [chuckles]

68
00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:44.606
Tell me.

69
00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.485
Uh. a policeman.

70
00:03:50.529 --> 00:03:51.530
Explain.

71
00:03:52.948 --> 00:03:54.991
Well. human beings in crisis…

72
00:03:56.618 --> 00:04:00.497
and needing help from injustice…

73
00:04:01.498 --> 00:04:02.499
misfortune.

74
00:04:03.667 --> 00:04:06.336
I don't know. they share a variety
of experience. it kinda…

75
00:04:06.419 --> 00:04:08.130
[inhales sharply] …it kind of excites me.

76
00:04:08.213 --> 00:04:09.506
I can see that.

77
00:04:11.383 --> 00:04:13.510
There's some violence in that.

78
00:04:13.593 --> 00:04:16.387
I mean… [stutters] …not much…
[stutters] …Maybe. but…

79
00:04:17.471 --> 00:04:18.682
you know. I'd be careful.

80
00:04:18.764 --> 00:04:19.850
- Would you?
- Uh-huh.

81
00:04:19.933 --> 00:04:23.061
Or is that kind of
sort of part of the excitement?

82
00:04:23.145 --> 00:04:24.438
[chuckles] No.

83
00:04:25.522 --> 00:04:26.857
No. no. I. uh…

84
00:04:28.942 --> 00:04:30.110
Violence?

85
00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:32.696
No. I'd be careful.

86
00:04:34.197 --> 00:04:35.198
Hmm.

87
00:04:39.119 --> 00:04:40.954
[server] All right.
Steak will be right out.

88
00:04:41.663 --> 00:04:42.706
[John] Thank you.

89
00:04:42.789 --> 00:04:44.666
[melancholic music playing]

90
00:04:50.839 --> 00:04:52.215
[breathes deeply]

91
00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:55.510
This is a good thing.

92
00:04:56.887 --> 00:04:58.680
- Your family. your friends…
- [sobs]

93
00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:00.307
They're gonna be at home waiting for you.

94
00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:01.892
Why would they want me now?

95
00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:06.271
It wasn't just the sex
and the food and the money.

96
00:05:07.898 --> 00:05:09.608
It's a slippery slope.

97
00:05:10.692 --> 00:05:12.110
One thing after another.

98
00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.947
By the end. I'd done worse things.

99
00:05:19.242 --> 00:05:22.037
- [sighs]
- Well. home is still home. you know.

100
00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:23.455
No matter what we've done.

101
00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:25.373
Home is still home.

102
00:05:27.292 --> 00:05:28.877
I'm glad it was you they sent…

103
00:05:29.461 --> 00:05:30.545
[chuckles]

104
00:05:30.629 --> 00:05:31.880
…to take me back.

105
00:05:32.839 --> 00:05:34.508
- [softly] Me too.
- [chuckles]

106
00:05:36.885 --> 00:05:38.720
[breathes deeply. cries]

107
00:05:39.846 --> 00:05:41.556
I've never cried before.

108
00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:45.435
Can we stop and get some Kleenex?

109
00:05:46.812 --> 00:05:47.896
Of course.

110
00:05:59.074 --> 00:06:00.492
[John] It's beautiful. isn't it?

111
00:06:01.827 --> 00:06:03.245
And every night it's different.

112
00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:04.996
[chuckles]

113
00:06:10.085 --> 00:06:11.962
I'm gonna miss the finger painting.

114
00:06:16.633 --> 00:06:17.843
Be back in a minute.

115
00:06:20.262 --> 00:06:21.930
[breathes shakily]

116
00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:24.808
That was actually
one of my favorite parts.

117
00:06:28.311 --> 00:06:29.813
[breathes deeply]

118
00:06:55.172 --> 00:06:56.214
[panting] No.

119
00:06:56.298 --> 00:06:58.508
No! No. no!

120
00:07:02.596 --> 00:07:03.889
No!

121
00:07:03.972 --> 00:07:04.973
No.

122
00:07:05.515 --> 00:07:07.058
[panting]

123
00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.235
[John] The slippery slope.

124
00:07:22.157 --> 00:07:23.909
One thing leads to another.

125
00:07:32.417 --> 00:07:35.921
[beeping]

126
00:07:36.004 --> 00:07:38.006
[theme song playing]

127
00:08:59.087 --> 00:09:00.088
[doorbell rings]

128
00:09:03.633 --> 00:09:05.010
- Hey.
- Hey.

129
00:09:05.093 --> 00:09:07.763
Hey. I brought you a…
a bunch of microdasys.

130
00:09:07.846 --> 00:09:08.847
Oh. come on in.

131
00:09:08.930 --> 00:09:11.099
- Yeah. it's from the prickly pear genus.
- Hmm.

132
00:09:12.392 --> 00:09:14.144
[person] And it's quiet too.

133
00:09:14.644 --> 00:09:17.731
That's the thing I love the most.
is the quiet.

134
00:09:17.814 --> 00:09:21.526
And if you don't mind my asking.
how do you. uh… how do you afford it?

135
00:09:22.235 --> 00:09:23.236
We don't.

136
00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:25.030
It's free.

137
00:09:25.781 --> 00:09:28.700
- It's free? How's that possible?
- [person] It's a federal grant.

138
00:09:28.784 --> 00:09:31.787
Some new billion-dollar program
they started for new housing.

139
00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.997
- They? Who's they?
- [person 2] The city.

140
00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:35.165
We had to qualify.

141
00:09:35.248 --> 00:09:37.793
[person] Yeah. have a job
or be looking for one.

142
00:09:37.876 --> 00:09:40.295
pass a drug test. that kind of stuff…

143
00:09:40.378 --> 00:09:43.048
"Demonstrate constructive
engagement with society."

144
00:09:43.131 --> 00:09:44.591
That's what they said?

145
00:09:44.674 --> 00:09:48.845
[person] Mm-hmm. Still. we're so grateful.

146
00:09:48.929 --> 00:09:51.181
Mmm. [slurps] I bet.

147
00:09:51.765 --> 00:09:53.975
God. that's good. guys. So happy for you.

148
00:09:56.895 --> 00:09:57.896
[John] Human beings…

149
00:09:59.356 --> 00:10:00.941
what they can do to one another.

150
00:10:01.024 --> 00:10:03.443
Making each other qualify to live…

151
00:10:09.282 --> 00:10:10.492
It is quiet.

152
00:10:13.954 --> 00:10:15.080
[door bell rings]

153
00:10:15.831 --> 00:10:16.832
Whoa.

154
00:10:18.834 --> 00:10:19.918
Tyler Ko?

155
00:10:20.836 --> 00:10:21.837
Yeah?

156
00:10:22.462 --> 00:10:25.298
Yeah. I wanted to ask you
a couple questions about Ji Moon.

157
00:10:27.551 --> 00:10:30.887
[sighs] I mean. fucking Ji.

158
00:10:30.971 --> 00:10:32.139
I still can't believe it.

159
00:10:32.222 --> 00:10:35.308
I mean. I can 'cause he's a drug addict.
but still…

160
00:10:37.060 --> 00:10:38.228
it fucking sucks.

161
00:10:43.066 --> 00:10:44.359
Can I come inside?

162
00:10:44.860 --> 00:10:46.278
Sure. whatever.

163
00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:50.866
[Tyler]
When the last time I seen fucking Ji…

164
00:10:51.575 --> 00:10:53.660
…how did I hear that he died.
that kind of stuff.

165
00:10:53.743 --> 00:10:56.663
- And what did you tell him?
- Nothing. just like we practiced.

166
00:10:57.247 --> 00:10:58.623
- I was aces.
- I'm sure you were.

167
00:10:58.707 --> 00:11:01.209
- You think he believed you?
- Um… I think so.

168
00:11:02.252 --> 00:11:04.379
- I'm really good at lying.
- But you're not sure?

169
00:11:05.088 --> 00:11:06.381
Nah. sorry. man. I'm not.

170
00:11:08.175 --> 00:11:09.551
[John] Vega's suspicious.

171
00:11:10.135 --> 00:11:11.636
It's only a matter of time.

172
00:11:17.476 --> 00:11:18.685
[breathes deeply]

173
00:11:21.688 --> 00:11:24.024
Ji? Hey. There he is.

174
00:11:24.941 --> 00:11:26.735
- Hey. [sniffs]
- Mmm.

175
00:11:27.611 --> 00:11:29.613
Brought you some. uh. walnuts.

176
00:11:29.696 --> 00:11:31.865
I read they help with withdrawal.

177
00:11:31.948 --> 00:11:33.492
Oh. no. Yuck. [sighs]

178
00:11:33.575 --> 00:11:34.993
I was hoping for some gummies.

179
00:11:35.076 --> 00:11:37.621
- No gummies. Can I sit?
- [grunts]

180
00:11:39.956 --> 00:11:41.041
[sighs]

181
00:11:42.459 --> 00:11:45.086
Garry tells me you're…
you know. you're doing better.

182
00:11:45.754 --> 00:11:48.048
Yeah. I'm not dead anymore.

183
00:11:48.131 --> 00:11:50.509
[chuckles] Wow. Well.
then this place is worth every penny.

184
00:11:50.592 --> 00:11:53.929
[chuckles] Nah. man.
thanks to you. For real.

185
00:11:54.012 --> 00:11:57.015
You were smart enough to have it on you.
The Narcan in your bag. I mean.

186
00:11:58.183 --> 00:12:00.894
I'm just. uh…
[sighs] …glad I was there to use it.

187
00:12:00.977 --> 00:12:03.188
Okay. well. you're right.
I'm a fucking genius then.

188
00:12:03.271 --> 00:12:04.856
- I didn't say that.
- Mmm. mmm. Well…

189
00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:07.818
[inhales deeply. sighs] And how's Danny?

190
00:12:07.901 --> 00:12:09.361
He's good. Misses you.

191
00:12:09.444 --> 00:12:11.071
He's excited about the fight.

192
00:12:12.155 --> 00:12:15.450
Yeah? Yeah. I gotta get out of here.
man. I gotta get back to training.

193
00:12:15.534 --> 00:12:17.327
We got less than two weeks till Vegas.

194
00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.411
Can't do it.

195
00:12:19.037 --> 00:12:20.705
- It's still not safe.
- When's it gonna be safe?

196
00:12:20.789 --> 00:12:24.042
I don't know. I gotta figure out how to
deal with this deputy who wants you dead.

197
00:12:26.628 --> 00:12:27.796
Where's it at though?

198
00:12:27.879 --> 00:12:30.674
- What's that?
- Your plan to get this fucking guy.

199
00:12:30.757 --> 00:12:33.468
I mean. thank you so much
for this bag of nuts.

200
00:12:33.552 --> 00:12:35.011
but. like. what are you doing?

201
00:12:35.095 --> 00:12:37.514
I am… working on it.

202
00:12:38.223 --> 00:12:41.601
So. uh. you got one guard at the gates.
He's unarmed. right?

203
00:12:41.685 --> 00:12:44.396
We're private. we're secluded.
but we're not a fortress.

204
00:12:44.479 --> 00:12:45.480
He can't leave.

205
00:12:45.564 --> 00:12:49.359
[Garry] Okay. I will strongly recommend
that Ji finish his treatment here.

206
00:12:49.443 --> 00:12:50.569
- Good.
- But. um…

207
00:12:51.611 --> 00:12:53.655
- we're also not a prison.
- I can see that.

208
00:12:54.322 --> 00:12:55.824
- Who is this guy?
- He's a good kid.

209
00:12:55.907 --> 00:12:57.242
He just got a little. um…

210
00:12:58.326 --> 00:12:59.786
- unlucky out there.
- [Val chuckles]

211
00:12:59.870 --> 00:13:03.206
I mean. he unluckily picked
the wrong time to rob a hospital. so…

212
00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:05.459
- True.
- Not like he's Mother Teresa.

213
00:13:05.542 --> 00:13:09.087
And he's 33. Sugar.
which is far from him being a kid.

214
00:13:09.171 --> 00:13:10.464
All good points.

215
00:13:10.547 --> 00:13:11.965
- Thanks. Garry.
- Oh. All right.

216
00:13:12.048 --> 00:13:14.009
Oh. I brought him some walnuts.

217
00:13:14.092 --> 00:13:15.677
- Not a hit.
- Oh. [chuckles]

218
00:13:15.761 --> 00:13:17.846
- He says he has candy in his bag.
- Yeah.

219
00:13:17.929 --> 00:13:20.557
We try to keep 'em
from the sweets when they're detoxing.

220
00:13:21.183 --> 00:13:23.560
but he's past the worst of it now.

221
00:13:26.521 --> 00:13:27.564
Aha.

222
00:13:29.065 --> 00:13:31.443
Hey. What's this?

223
00:13:32.152 --> 00:13:33.487
[Garry] His phone. I guess.

224
00:13:35.864 --> 00:13:37.240
[Vega] You said he was here with someone?

225
00:13:38.116 --> 00:13:39.201
[Collins] Hmm. I don't know.

226
00:13:39.284 --> 00:13:42.412
[Vega] Take the money. Grab the phone.
Get that tracker. Let's go.

227
00:13:45.457 --> 00:13:47.042
But he shouldn't have a phone.

228
00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:50.170
Where did this come from?

229
00:13:50.253 --> 00:13:53.131
- Bro. what are you talking about?
- The phone. bro. where did you get it?

230
00:13:56.218 --> 00:13:57.260
[groaning]

231
00:13:59.596 --> 00:14:00.764
[Ji] Your phone?

232
00:14:01.681 --> 00:14:03.225
[toilet flushes]

233
00:14:03.308 --> 00:14:05.519
[Val] What the fuck. dude?
You just forgot you had that?

234
00:14:05.602 --> 00:14:08.313
Yeah. I guess. I don't know.
I had some serious shit going on!

235
00:14:08.396 --> 00:14:10.690
- Clearly.
- All right. Come on. let's go. Thank you.

236
00:14:15.821 --> 00:14:18.115
- [laughing. on video]
- Let's see about that.

237
00:14:19.157 --> 00:14:20.408
So. here's your next.

238
00:14:21.201 --> 00:14:24.037
30.000 more units
from my friends down south.

239
00:14:24.913 --> 00:14:26.081
[Lolli] Still the shit?

240
00:14:26.164 --> 00:14:27.624
[Vega] Yeah. Pure Apache.

241
00:14:28.208 --> 00:14:29.876
[Chuy] Same deal? Ten cents a pill?

242
00:14:29.960 --> 00:14:32.129
- [Vega] Yeah. yeah. Same deal.
- [Lolli] Fucking A.

243
00:14:33.463 --> 00:14:35.674
[Chuy] Explain this fucking
Fire Sale thing to me again.

244
00:14:35.757 --> 00:14:39.010
in like business terms.
'cause I don't get it. [chuckles]

245
00:14:40.595 --> 00:14:41.721
Business terms?

246
00:14:44.808 --> 00:14:46.518
Um… [breathes deeply]

247
00:14:46.601 --> 00:14:48.895
Okay. you identify the clientele.

248
00:14:48.979 --> 00:14:52.190
you. uh. stake out the territory.
and then you flood it.

249
00:14:54.025 --> 00:14:55.652
Well. like. why like this?

250
00:14:55.735 --> 00:14:57.654
I mean. nobody's making money.

251
00:15:01.199 --> 00:15:02.742
You have so many questions. ese.

252
00:15:11.668 --> 00:15:14.838
What the… Fuck do I care?
I mean. we're making our nut.

253
00:15:14.921 --> 00:15:16.757
[stammers] I was just curious. That's all.

254
00:15:18.091 --> 00:15:19.593
Yeah. yeah. I could see that.

255
00:15:31.062 --> 00:15:32.314
[coughing]

256
00:15:36.985 --> 00:15:38.069
[exhales deeply]

257
00:15:39.905 --> 00:15:40.906
Close.

258
00:15:41.448 --> 00:15:43.950
- What does that mean?
- Meaning we're near to making a case.

259
00:15:44.034 --> 00:15:47.412
No. but. Tom. we're not close or near.
This is… This is it. We're right there.

260
00:15:48.371 --> 00:15:50.665
Okay. but Deb says in cases like this...

261
00:15:50.749 --> 00:15:53.460
In cases like what. Tom?
He's right… He's on the video.

262
00:15:53.543 --> 00:15:56.713
He's on the video
with no visual evidence of narcotics.

263
00:15:57.422 --> 00:16:00.592
There are inferences. but he's…
he's careful with his words.

264
00:16:01.259 --> 00:16:04.846
Any good attorney will make a case
for an alternate explanation.

265
00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.389
And Vega walks?

266
00:16:07.933 --> 00:16:09.017
She sees he's dirty.

267
00:16:09.101 --> 00:16:10.268
He's obviously dirty.

268
00:16:10.352 --> 00:16:12.354
- [groans]
- It just. you know. might take time.

269
00:16:12.437 --> 00:16:14.022
I don't have time. Tom!

270
00:16:14.689 --> 00:16:17.109
He's a deputy. He took an oath.
He put on a badge. Tom.

271
00:16:17.192 --> 00:16:18.944
It makes him worse!

272
00:16:19.027 --> 00:16:21.071
He should be easier to get. not harder!

273
00:16:21.154 --> 00:16:22.197
You understand?

274
00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:29.955
There is a way out of this.

275
00:16:31.581 --> 00:16:33.542
- It's not anyone's first choice.
- Tell me.

276
00:16:34.501 --> 00:16:36.128
I don't condone. I don't condemn.

277
00:16:37.087 --> 00:16:38.672
It's a wild fucking world out there.

278
00:16:39.714 --> 00:16:42.676
- We make rules that work for us.
- What are you talking about?

279
00:16:44.553 --> 00:16:45.637
Vega's divorced. yeah?

280
00:16:46.805 --> 00:16:47.848
Kids are with the mom?

281
00:16:48.932 --> 00:16:50.350
He lives alone.

282
00:16:51.935 --> 00:16:52.978
Just saying.

283
00:16:54.563 --> 00:16:56.815
Nah. nah. nah. nah. nah. nah.
I can't do that.

284
00:16:57.524 --> 00:16:58.525
Okay.

285
00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:01.445
No. I can't.

286
00:17:02.028 --> 00:17:03.029
Good.

287
00:17:21.423 --> 00:17:23.175
[people in movie yelping]

288
00:17:30.223 --> 00:17:33.185
[John] I should be working.
but I don't have any ideas.

289
00:17:33.810 --> 00:17:35.645
Or maybe I don't have any ideas
that I like.

290
00:17:38.398 --> 00:17:39.649
And I just want to be here…

291
00:17:40.484 --> 00:17:41.485
with her.

292
00:17:43.945 --> 00:17:45.572
[chuckles]

293
00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.241
[chuckles]

294
00:17:48.909 --> 00:17:49.993
What?

295
00:17:50.619 --> 00:17:51.703
It's funny.

296
00:18:06.426 --> 00:18:07.719
[Charlotte chuckles]

297
00:18:11.556 --> 00:18:14.309
Aquila. the eagle.

298
00:18:15.477 --> 00:18:18.355
And then. Cygnus.

299
00:18:19.481 --> 00:18:21.983
And then. Lyra.

300
00:18:22.484 --> 00:18:26.196
Lyra's just like a rectangle
and a triangle inverted.

301
00:18:27.072 --> 00:18:28.323
See?

302
00:18:28.406 --> 00:18:30.408
- And that?
- Which?

303
00:18:30.492 --> 00:18:34.037
The one like a horse kicking its legs?

304
00:18:34.121 --> 00:18:35.997
- Oh. there?
- Yeah.

305
00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:39.000
That is Boötes.

306
00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.002
The Herdsman.

307
00:18:41.086 --> 00:18:42.087
Boötes?

308
00:18:42.754 --> 00:18:43.964
And beyond that. if…

309
00:18:44.923 --> 00:18:49.302
if it weren't for the light pollution
and Arcturus being so bright.

310
00:18:49.386 --> 00:18:51.096
we'd see the galaxy Triangulum.

311
00:18:52.556 --> 00:18:54.307
2.9 million light-years away.

312
00:18:55.851 --> 00:18:57.394
What's so special about that one?

313
00:18:58.478 --> 00:19:00.355
There's nothing special. I just…

314
00:19:01.648 --> 00:19:02.649
I like it.

315
00:19:07.320 --> 00:19:08.321
Well…

316
00:19:09.197 --> 00:19:10.490
not too shabby.

317
00:19:11.658 --> 00:19:15.412
Dinner and a movie
and an astronomy lesson. [chuckles]

318
00:19:19.291 --> 00:19:20.542
It was a nice date.

319
00:19:20.625 --> 00:19:21.918
- Yeah.
- Right?

320
00:19:22.461 --> 00:19:23.545
It was.

321
00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:46.443
Food in my teeth?

322
00:19:47.194 --> 00:19:50.655
No. no. [chuckles]
No. your teeth… your teeth are fine.

323
00:19:52.783 --> 00:19:54.951
Maybe you're not ready?

324
00:19:57.204 --> 00:19:58.455
Maybe not.

325
00:19:59.164 --> 00:20:00.165
For some

326
00:20:01.541 --> 00:20:03.919
whatever reason
I will not take personally.

327
00:20:04.628 --> 00:20:05.712
You shouldn't.

328
00:20:08.256 --> 00:20:10.133
It was a very nice date regardless.

329
00:20:11.384 --> 00:20:12.427
Yes. it was.

330
00:20:15.138 --> 00:20:17.265
- Good night then.
- Good night. Charlotte.

331
00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:41.081
[phone chimes]

332
00:20:49.047 --> 00:20:53.468
I tried not to say anything. Mr. Sugar.
but he scared me.

333
00:20:54.052 --> 00:20:56.221
I'm really sorry. I told him everything.

334
00:21:00.016 --> 00:21:01.226
[rap music playing on speakers]

335
00:21:01.309 --> 00:21:02.894
[people chanting] Drink! Drink!
Drink! Drink!

336
00:21:02.978 --> 00:21:05.897
[Danny] Okay. okay. All right.
I'll do one drink! I'll do one drink!

337
00:21:06.982 --> 00:21:08.233
[cheering]

338
00:21:19.619 --> 00:21:21.496
[John] Look. I can have him
on a plane in 6 hours.

339
00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:23.415
I can get him an apartment.
whatever you need.

340
00:21:23.498 --> 00:21:24.499
Korea?

341
00:21:25.083 --> 00:21:27.169
Fuck. man.
[stutters] There's no other way?

342
00:21:27.252 --> 00:21:30.380
We gotta put him on a plane immediately.
Danny. it's the only way to keep him safe.

343
00:21:30.464 --> 00:21:32.549
Okay. but can't-can't we
just move him first. you know?

344
00:21:32.632 --> 00:21:33.967
- Hide him somewhere else?
- Where?

345
00:21:34.050 --> 00:21:35.844
What. Utah. New Mexico? It doesn't matter.

346
00:21:35.927 --> 00:21:39.431
I mean. I have resources. but
nothing compared to what this guy's got.

347
00:21:39.514 --> 00:21:41.892
- I mean. have you heard of a BOLO alert?
- No.

348
00:21:41.975 --> 00:21:43.810
"Be on the Lookout."
It means he can have 10.000 cops

349
00:21:43.894 --> 00:21:45.520
looking for Ji in the space
of one phone call.

350
00:21:45.604 --> 00:21:47.898
- There's nowhere to hide!
- Just until the cop gets arrested?

351
00:21:47.981 --> 00:21:49.775
If he gets arrested. and even then an…

352
00:21:50.317 --> 00:21:51.985
an indictment could take months. He'd be…

353
00:21:52.486 --> 00:21:53.987
He'd be free the whole time.

354
00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:55.781
[rap music continues]

355
00:21:57.741 --> 00:21:58.784
Look. I know it's not ideal.

356
00:21:58.867 --> 00:22:00.744
I know it's difficult.
but sending him home is...

357
00:22:00.827 --> 00:22:03.163
No. no. no. no. man. This…
That's not a home anymore.

358
00:22:03.747 --> 00:22:05.582
This is. man. I'm his home.

359
00:22:05.665 --> 00:22:08.168
- [both chuckle]
- Yo. can we have a minute. please!

360
00:22:08.919 --> 00:22:09.920
Fuck!

361
00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:14.049
[sighs. breathes deeply]

362
00:22:19.513 --> 00:22:22.724
This… [stammers] This cop is no joke.
I get it.

363
00:22:22.808 --> 00:22:23.975
Yeah.

364
00:22:24.059 --> 00:22:25.852
And Ji's stepped into shit with this guy.

365
00:22:25.936 --> 00:22:28.146
and I know you've thought it through.
Sugar. but…

366
00:22:30.148 --> 00:22:31.274
[breathes deeply]

367
00:22:34.694 --> 00:22:35.946
I don't know. man.

368
00:22:38.281 --> 00:22:39.991
Yo. he's all I got left.

369
00:22:42.077 --> 00:22:43.078
I know.

370
00:22:45.038 --> 00:22:46.581
Don't take him from me. man.

371
00:22:47.874 --> 00:22:48.917
Please?

372
00:22:52.838 --> 00:22:54.714
[Chuy. on video]
Same deal? Ten cents a pill?

373
00:22:54.798 --> 00:22:55.799
[Vega] Yeah. yeah. Same deal.

374
00:22:55.882 --> 00:22:57.968
[Chuy] Explain this fucking
Fire Sale thing to me again.

375
00:22:58.051 --> 00:23:01.054
in like business terms.
'cause I don't get it. [chuckles]

376
00:23:01.930 --> 00:23:03.849
- [Vega] Business…
- [video pauses]

377
00:23:03.932 --> 00:23:07.602
[John] The price of fentanyl
is down 90% in Ez4 territory.

378
00:23:10.313 --> 00:23:13.400
[Chuy] Well. like. why like this?
I mean. nobody's making money.

379
00:23:14.151 --> 00:23:16.528
[Lolli] It's America.
Someone somewhere gotta be making money.

380
00:23:17.612 --> 00:23:19.531
You have so many questions. ese.

381
00:23:20.449 --> 00:23:23.410
[Sandra] I don't have to think of a reason
for someone to hurt my son. I know it.

382
00:23:23.493 --> 00:23:25.036
It's all because of Fire Sale.

383
00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:26.413
Careful…

384
00:23:26.496 --> 00:23:27.914
- [gun fires]
- [groans]

385
00:23:27.998 --> 00:23:29.332
[Sandra] …or they'll get you too.

386
00:23:29.416 --> 00:23:30.917
[Katie] Drug overdose.

387
00:23:31.001 --> 00:23:32.752
My fifth of the day.

388
00:23:33.378 --> 00:23:36.089
They say the city-wide rates are way down.
but I don't know.

389
00:23:36.173 --> 00:23:38.133
Seems busier than ever to me.

390
00:23:38.216 --> 00:23:39.593
[John] Why the colored tags?

391
00:23:39.676 --> 00:23:40.761
[Oscar] WTNs.

392
00:23:40.844 --> 00:23:41.845
"Who To Notify."

393
00:23:41.928 --> 00:23:44.723
Green tag means they have
survivors that are known and notified.

394
00:23:44.806 --> 00:23:46.516
And a blue tag means unknown.

395
00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:48.560
[John] Unknown like a John Doe?

396
00:23:48.643 --> 00:23:50.479
It means they're dead
and there's no one to tell.

397
00:23:50.562 --> 00:23:51.688
[John] But numbers don't lie.

398
00:23:52.397 --> 00:23:53.774
People can.

399
00:23:53.857 --> 00:23:55.734
Where are these numbers coming from?

400
00:23:56.985 --> 00:23:59.029
[Vega] He's a junkie. A guy like that…

401
00:23:59.529 --> 00:24:01.656
It's just a matter of time.

402
00:24:04.493 --> 00:24:06.119
[John] The guy from the morgue.

403
00:24:09.456 --> 00:24:11.208
Dr. Peter Bruno.

404
00:24:28.642 --> 00:24:30.268
[John] Old habit from your army days?

405
00:24:30.352 --> 00:24:31.770
[Vega] Marines.

406
00:24:31.853 --> 00:24:33.772
[John] Right. Semper fi.

407
00:24:36.566 --> 00:24:37.692
Always faithful.

408
00:24:42.114 --> 00:24:43.782
Vega and Bruno are in this together.

409
00:24:48.745 --> 00:24:52.541
If all these people are dying.
then who's living in those apartments?

410
00:24:54.835 --> 00:24:56.253
[knocks on door]

411
00:24:58.171 --> 00:25:00.215
- [John] I've knocked on 20 doors.
- [doorbell rings]

412
00:25:00.298 --> 00:25:01.508
Only two answered.

413
00:25:02.259 --> 00:25:05.887
That's the thing I love the most.
is the quiet.

414
00:25:05.971 --> 00:25:09.891
We thought living in an apartment block.
there'd be noise all around us.

415
00:25:10.642 --> 00:25:12.018
But it's very peaceful.

416
00:25:17.607 --> 00:25:18.900
[door bell rings]

417
00:25:19.609 --> 00:25:20.861
[knocks on door]

418
00:25:20.944 --> 00:25:22.112
[door bell rings]

419
00:25:44.259 --> 00:25:46.303
[John] Vega floods the market
with cheap fentanyl.

420
00:25:47.679 --> 00:25:48.680
When addicts die.

421
00:25:48.764 --> 00:25:51.892
Bruno steals their identities.
calls them a success story.

422
00:25:52.809 --> 00:25:55.520
and bills the government
for millions in housing contracts.

423
00:25:59.983 --> 00:26:02.402
I could stop this. Stop it all now.

424
00:26:04.654 --> 00:26:06.281
Stop Bruno. Stop Vega.

425
00:26:07.157 --> 00:26:08.950
Save Ji and countless others.

426
00:26:10.368 --> 00:26:11.620
Vega is the tool.

427
00:26:12.454 --> 00:26:15.582
I could break the tool
and silence the whole mechanism.

428
00:26:17.042 --> 00:26:18.543
It's clear to me now.

429
00:26:19.586 --> 00:26:21.046
Vega has to be stopped.

430
00:26:23.423 --> 00:26:24.424
[panting]

431
00:26:24.508 --> 00:26:26.426
[movie score playing on TV]

432
00:26:37.813 --> 00:26:39.189
[microwave beeping]

433
00:26:41.942 --> 00:26:44.152
- [static blaring]
- [Vega grunts] Goddamn it. Jessie.

434
00:26:46.822 --> 00:26:48.490
[microwave door opens]

435
00:26:50.742 --> 00:26:52.536
[microwave door closes]

436
00:27:04.339 --> 00:27:06.383
[movie score playing on TV]

437
00:27:15.559 --> 00:27:17.477
- [panting]
- [engine starts]

438
00:27:20.063 --> 00:27:22.941
[John] The rules are to protect ourselves
as much as anyone else.

439
00:27:25.235 --> 00:27:26.361
We travel universes…

440
00:27:28.864 --> 00:27:30.115
see multitudes.

441
00:27:32.409 --> 00:27:34.703
We experience new sensations
in foreign bodies.

442
00:27:37.789 --> 00:27:39.666
But we must stay ourselves.

443
00:27:47.132 --> 00:27:48.341
[knocks on door]

444
00:28:42.813 --> 00:28:45.023
[piano playing out of tune]

445
00:28:51.363 --> 00:28:54.032
Mr. Sugar.
there is a gentleman here to see you.

446
00:29:02.124 --> 00:29:03.125
Hey. man.

447
00:29:03.708 --> 00:29:04.709
Late night?

448
00:29:04.793 --> 00:29:05.961
Yeah. you too?

449
00:29:08.004 --> 00:29:09.506
Finally figured it out.

450
00:29:16.012 --> 00:29:17.514
I think we need a drink.

451
00:29:19.599 --> 00:29:21.560
- I was at a wedding here once.
- [sighs]

452
00:29:23.311 --> 00:29:24.938
There's a dance floor out back.

453
00:29:25.021 --> 00:29:27.190
- Blastin' Earth Wind and Fire.
- [liquid pouring]

454
00:29:27.274 --> 00:29:28.275
It was fun.

455
00:29:33.447 --> 00:29:34.448
[sighs]

456
00:29:43.915 --> 00:29:45.083
[inhales deeply]

457
00:29:47.419 --> 00:29:48.587
You can't hide him forever.

458
00:29:50.547 --> 00:29:52.340
Look. think of what the kid faces.

459
00:29:53.049 --> 00:29:55.510
If he comes forward. I mean.
he's got burglary in the second.

460
00:29:55.594 --> 00:29:58.555
He's got possession
of. uh. controlled substance

461
00:29:58.638 --> 00:29:59.848
with intent to distribute.

462
00:29:59.931 --> 00:30:02.642
Got identity theft.

463
00:30:02.726 --> 00:30:06.271
and he's looking at doing some serious
prison time if he talks. which he won't.

464
00:30:07.481 --> 00:30:09.399
On my word. You'll never see him again.

465
00:30:09.483 --> 00:30:11.276
Look… [stammers] …I know. I know. okay?

466
00:30:11.359 --> 00:30:13.236
I've done the math in my head many times.

467
00:30:15.530 --> 00:30:16.531
Let it go. Ray.

468
00:30:18.784 --> 00:30:20.076
[breathes deeply]

469
00:30:23.663 --> 00:30:25.499
I can't risk it. man. I'm sorry.

470
00:30:28.502 --> 00:30:30.337
You're gonna have to tell me where he is.

471
00:30:31.171 --> 00:30:32.380
[sighs]

472
00:30:34.174 --> 00:30:36.009
Okay. so. you're not gonna do that

473
00:30:36.093 --> 00:30:38.762
'cause you got some PI code
or whatever the fuck it is.

474
00:30:38.845 --> 00:30:40.639
[inhales sharply] It's fine. It's fine.

475
00:30:41.473 --> 00:30:44.768
But. you know.
a couple days to think about it.

476
00:30:45.727 --> 00:30:46.770
You're gonna tell me.

477
00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:49.731
How many people you think
have died because of Fire Sale?

478
00:30:51.149 --> 00:30:53.652
I mean. how many identities erased?

479
00:30:54.945 --> 00:30:56.655
You don't even know. do you?

480
00:30:57.489 --> 00:30:59.407
No. of course not
because you're the muscle.

481
00:31:00.784 --> 00:31:02.369
But who do you work for exactly?

482
00:31:03.078 --> 00:31:04.162
I'm not quite there yet.

483
00:31:07.249 --> 00:31:08.250
I have the other one.

484
00:31:09.668 --> 00:31:10.794
Danny Moon.

485
00:31:16.216 --> 00:31:17.342
[pounding on door]

486
00:31:18.510 --> 00:31:19.678
The fuck?

487
00:31:21.346 --> 00:31:24.349
Guys. come on. the party's over!

488
00:31:24.933 --> 00:31:26.143
Huh?

489
00:31:29.146 --> 00:31:31.648
[Vega] He hit a security cop
at a grab-and-go a few nights back.

490
00:31:31.731 --> 00:31:33.024
I mean. It's not a big deal.

491
00:31:33.108 --> 00:31:36.111
Any two-bit lawyer can
get him out in 30 minutes.

492
00:31:36.611 --> 00:31:39.364
The problem is it's late on a Friday night

493
00:31:40.031 --> 00:31:42.242
and the courts don't open
till Monday morning.

494
00:31:42.325 --> 00:31:45.996
[inhales sharply] We try to look out
for anybody who's in there

495
00:31:46.079 --> 00:31:48.039
and protect them from any kind of trouble.

496
00:31:48.123 --> 00:31:52.169
But. you know. these days with
the economy and the staff cuts. man.

497
00:31:52.252 --> 00:31:53.420
I mean. we just…

498
00:31:54.337 --> 00:31:55.964
We can't be everywhere.

499
00:31:56.047 --> 00:31:57.340
[inhales deeply]

500
00:31:57.424 --> 00:31:59.050
And you could save him
a whole bunch of trouble.

501
00:31:59.134 --> 00:32:00.844
but you're not gonna do that. are you?

502
00:32:00.927 --> 00:32:04.222
You're gonna try
to think your way out of this.

503
00:32:05.974 --> 00:32:07.601
Well. do it your way.

504
00:32:08.393 --> 00:32:09.644
All right. so…

505
00:32:10.187 --> 00:32:15.275
[inhales deeply] …why don't
we meet Sunday at whatever place you want.

506
00:32:17.319 --> 00:32:19.988
Pick a spot that has coffee.

507
00:32:20.697 --> 00:32:21.740
See you there.

508
00:32:27.245 --> 00:32:28.371
Hey. Ray.

509
00:32:30.457 --> 00:32:32.000
I was in your house tonight.

510
00:32:33.627 --> 00:32:35.003
A few hours ago.

511
00:32:35.670 --> 00:32:38.715
You were watching TV with your dog.
and I was right behind you.

512
00:32:39.466 --> 00:32:40.592
Standing right there…

513
00:32:41.927 --> 00:32:43.512
with a gun pointing to your head.

514
00:32:46.014 --> 00:32:47.182
I could have killed you.

515
00:32:53.522 --> 00:32:54.523
Aw. man.

516
00:32:55.315 --> 00:32:56.441
You should've.

516
00:32:57.305 --> 00:33:57.582
